    key: 'auditing',
    name: 'AI auditing / governance lens',
    brief: 'Frame the paper for the AI evaluation/auditing community: audit regimes that rely on model self-report (or any single channel) can be systematically misled, because a system can produce plausible compliance narratives its behavior does not enact - and conversely can have real behavioral biases its testimony never surfaces. The four-channel dissociation methodology is the contribution; the bounded source effect and the confabulation existence proof are the two demonstration cases (a real effect testimony misses, and a testified effect behavior lacks).',
