    key: 'odd-robust',
    name: 'The odd-robust-finding lens',
    brief: 'Center the paradox the author flagged: the one source-dependence effect that survives the reliability audit is domain-specific (it appears on AI topics - the model\'s own domain - not on carbon tax etc.), qualitatively stable but quantitatively unstable, and introspectively inaccessible (the model confabulates effects elsewhere and does not report the real one). What kind of phenomenon is that? Build the framing that makes THIS the research question: characterizing when and where source-dependence is real, and why self-relevant topics differ. Be careful: the topic-specificity evidence base may be thin - state exactly what additional evidence this framing needs.',
